_≡ƒöÆ Security & Privacy_ | _≡ƒö┤ Critical_ | _ΓÜí Quick win_

**Validate the version string before you join it into a path.**

`version_install_dir` at Line 64 joins the caller-supplied `version` with no validation, and `version_binary` builds on it. `Path::join` treats `..` as a real parent traversal and lets an absolute component discard the base entirely.

The reachable write primitive is the install path. `src/nu/bootstrap.rs` Lines 225-238 use these helpers to `create_dir_all`, `std::fs::copy` a binary, `make_executable`, and write a `VERSION` file. The `version` value arrives from the CLI positional in `src/cmd/setup.rs` Lines 37-39. So `numan setup nu ../../../../tmp/pwn` writes an executable outside `$NUMAN_ROOT`. `numan use <version>` reaches `write_active_version` and `is_version_installed` with the same unvalidated string.

Validate once, here, and reject anything that is not a plain semantic version. Do it in the helper rather than at each call site, so a future caller cannot reintroduce the hole.

Two smaller points in the same segment. `versioned_nu_dir` at Line 58-60 returns the same path as `bootstrap::managed_nu_dir`; two names for one directory is how the "remove the managed directory and lose every version" behaviour stayed invisible. The binary-name expression at Line 69 is repeated at Line 102 and duplicates `bootstrap::nu_binary_name()`; collapse the three into one.





Based on coding guidelines: "Identify and fix security issues when encountered, including injection, XSS, SQL injection, path traversal, and secret leakage." and "`numan install` must write only to `$NUMAN_ROOT`".

<details>
<summary>≡ƒ¢í∩╕Å Proposed fix: reject non-semver version components</summary>

```diff
+/// Validate a version string that will become a path component.
+///
+/// Rejects traversal, separators, and absolute components before any join.
+pub fn validate_version_component(version: &str) -> Result<()> {
+    if semver::Version::parse(version).is_err() {
+        bail!("Invalid Nu version '{version}'. Expected a semantic version such as 0.113.1.");
+    }
+    Ok(())
+}
+
 /// Directory for a specific Nu version install.
-pub fn version_install_dir(root: &Path, version: &str) -> PathBuf {
-    versioned_nu_dir(root).join(version)
-}
+pub fn version_install_dir(root: &Path, version: &str) -> Result<PathBuf> {
+    validate_version_component(version)?;
+    Ok(versioned_nu_dir(root).join(version))
+}

 /// Binary path for a specific Nu version.
-pub fn version_binary(root: &Path, version: &str) -> PathBuf {
-    let binary_name = if cfg!(windows) { "nu.exe" } else { "nu" };
-    version_install_dir(root, version).join(binary_name)
-}
+pub fn version_binary(root: &Path, version: &str) -> Result<PathBuf> {
+    Ok(version_install_dir(root, version)?.join(nu_binary_name()))
+}
```

Note that `semver::Version::parse` rejects a bare `0.113`, so confirm every real Nushell release tag parses before you adopt this exact predicate.
</details>

